cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite the paper."
title: >-
  Unbounded Timing Terms Make a Composite Accident-Anticipation Score
  Video-Blind: Evidence from a Live Benchmark
abstract: >-
  A constant risk score that reads no pixels scores 2.35291 on the private
  leaderboard of a live accident-anticipation benchmark, matching the
  eighth-placed team of thirteen. Twenty-five video-blind submissions, designed
  so that unknown terms cancel under differencing, decompose the metric from
  outside the competition without access to any label, and establish that the
  benchmark's published formula does not reproduce its own scorer.
